.TH KRATER 1 "July 2026" "Krater Pro" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
krater \- evidence-native coding agent powered by the Krater API
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B krater
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIPROMPT\fR]
.br
.B krater setup
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.br
.B krater doctor
[\fB--json\fR] [\fB--live\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Krater Pro provides an interactive coding agent, durable verified tasks, and a
loopback-only local web IDE. Project state, evidence, policies, and caches stay
local. Krater inference requires network access and a Krater-issued credential.
.SH FIRST RUN
Run \fBkrater setup\fR in the project you want to use. The interactive setup
accepts the credential without terminal echo and prefers the operating-system
credential store. Run \fBkrater doctor\fR to validate local readiness.
.SH COMMON COMMANDS
.TP
.B krater setup
Configure and validate a Krater credential without placing it in process
arguments.
.TP
.B krater doctor
Check runtime, credential source, Git, workspace, sandbox, and local evidence
storage readiness. Add \fB--live\fR only when an authenticated API check is
intended.
.TP
.B krater web
Start the local IDE on a loopback address.
.TP
.B krater completion bash|zsh|fish
Generate a shell completion script.
.TP
.B krater task --help
Show durable task planning, execution, verification, and publication commands.
.SH SECURITY
Never put an API key on the command line. Prefer \fBkrater setup\fR or an
ephemeral \fBKRATER_API_KEY\fR environment value. External mutations require
structured authorization and receipts.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I .krater/
Ignored local task events, evidence, transactions, and verified caches.
.TP
.I .krater-intent/
Optional version-controlled intent and policy artifacts.
.TP
.I .env
Owner-private plaintext fallback only when explicitly selected.
.SH SEE ALSO
Full documentation:
https://github.com/SupratimSircar05/krater-pro/tree/main/docs
